          "type": "public-claim-domain",
          "old": "The Unruh state is a different state, defined on the right exterior together with the black-hole interior of $\\mathcal S_{\\rm ext}$.",
          "new": "The Unruh state is a different state on the connected open domain $\\mathcal D_U:=\\{(T,X)\\in\\mathbb R^2:X^2-T^2>-1,\\ T+X>0\\}\\times S^2$ of $\\mathcal S_{\\rm ext}$. Define $\\mathcal H_R^+:=\\{T=X>0\\}\\times S^2$ and $\\mathcal B:=\\{(T,X)\\in\\mathbb R^2:T>|X|,\\ X^2-T^2>-1\\}\\times S^2$; then $\\mathcal D_U=\\mathcal E_R\\cup\\mathcal H_R^+\\cup\\mathcal B$, and every point of the right future horizon has an open neighborhood in this domain."
