      "changes": [
        {
          "type": "public-formulation-covariance",
          "old": "A covariant prescription here has the supplied local-covariance property: its assigned local data commute with pullback under time-orientation-preserving isometric embeddings with causally convex image.",
          "new": "A covariant prescription here has the supplied local-covariance property: its assigned local data commute with pullback under smooth time-orientation-preserving isometric embeddings $\\psi:(M,g)\\to(M',g')$ with causally convex image that preserve the prescribed scalar potential, $V=\\psi^*V'$, comparing the same scale $\\mu$ and finite normalization conditions $\\mathbf c$. Potential preservation is equivalently $P(\\psi^*f)=\\psi^*(P'f)$ for every $f\\in C^\\infty(M')$. This assigns no preferred state; covariance of stress expectations is required only for supplied states whose two-point distributions satisfy $W_\\omega=(\\psi\\times\\psi)^*W_{\\omega'}$."
        }
      ],
